book></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKITO SHIZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYASHITA, SATORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NODA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMODA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAGA, YASUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKITO, SHIZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A red EL (10R), a green EL (10G) and a blue EL (10B) for emitting red, green and blue light are arranged on the back of liquid crystal display elements (11R, 11G and 11B) that display primary colors, respectively. The ELs are organic EL elements that include organic luminescent film. Each of the EL elements comprises an organic luminescent layer (14) interposed between ITO electrodes (13) and metal electrodes (15), which are in the form of mutually perpendicular stripes, and light is emitted from the intersections (luminescent points) of the stripes of the ITO and metal electrodes. The luminescent points are arranged two-dimensionally on a glass substrate (12) to illuminate the whole display area of the liquid crystal display elements.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Une EL rouge (10R), une EL verte (10G) et une EL bleue (10B) conçues pour émettre respectivement de la lumière rouge, verte et bleue, sont placées à l'arrière d'éléments d'affichage à cristaux liquides (11R, 11G et 11B) qui affichent respectivement les couleurs primaires. Les EL sont des éléments EL organiques qui comprennent une couche organique luminescente. Chaque élément EL est constitué d'une couche organique luminescente (14) placée entre des électrodes ITO (13) et des électrodes métalliques qui se présentent sous la forme de bandes perpendiculaires les unes aux autres, et la lumière est émise depuis les intersections (points luminescents) des bandes électrodes ITO et métalliques. Les points luminescents sont disposés en deux dimensions sur un substrat de verre (12), de manière qu'ils illuminent la zone d'affichage intégrale des éléments d'affichage à cristaux liquides.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>